<StilArticle Eyebrow="Blog" EyebrowHref="#blog" Title="Five rules for a calm Monday" HeadingLevel="3"
             Lead="The week is decided on Friday afternoon."
             Author="Maja Lind" Date="new DateTime(2026, 11, 3)" ReadingTime="5 min read"
             Image="images/post-monday.svg" ImageAlt="A week in the planner, with tasks over five days"
             Caption="A week planned on Friday."
             Contents="@([new StilLinkItem("Why Mondays go wrong", "#why-mondays"), new StilLinkItem("The five rules", "#five-rules")])"
             Tags="@([new StilLinkItem("Planning", "#planning")])">
    <p>Every team we talk to has the same Monday: the first hour goes to working out who does what.</p>
    <h4 id="why-mondays">Why Mondays go wrong</h4>
    <p>A plan made on Monday morning is made under pressure, with half the facts.</p>
    <h4 id="five-rules">The five rules</h4>
    <ol>
        <li>Book the shared things first.</li>
        <li>Put time off in the plan.</li>
        <li>Leave a fifth of each day empty.</li>
    </ol>
</StilArticle>
